            "line": 9,
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "line": 10,
            "text": "The hosting HTTP adapter authenticates the caller and supplies a trusted `principal` containing their user and tenant IDs. Request parameters remain caller-controlled. Authentication itself is outside this sample; the principal is not populated from request parameters or an unverified token."
          },
          {
            "line": 11,
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "line": 12,
            "text": "Entry points are in `src/http.ts`. Application queries and the in-memory repository represent the application and persistence boundaries. Responses use HTTP-style status codes, but no server or database is required. The repository is initialized with rows by its caller; no external service is contacted."
